;; Clojure's AOT level's divergences (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, REAP1, RPS3, RPS4, RPS16): the
;; classes of the level's non-passes, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format (test/clojure/
;; divergences.edn says how a case is written and matched). The level's check is Clojure's suite
;; compiled (REAP3, test/arbace-go-aot-results.edn); beside it diffcheck's Clojure
;; pair (bin/diffcheck, test/diffcheck/known.edn: the evaluated half against the compiled one),
;; its known disagreements as cases "known REASON". Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :interned-at-load
  :title "compiled code interns the vars it names when its namespace's loader starts"
  :kind :design
  :why "as the JVM's AOT: a compiled loader makes its constants, the vars they name among them, when it starts (Compiler$AOT/pool), so fresh.ns/fv, scratch.space/in-scratch and user/map exist before the cases that define them; evaluated code interns a var when the form naming it is analyzed. Recorded as known (doc/FUTAMURA-SURVEY.md, \"One-segment namespaces\", \"F3 and F4 measured together\"); no decision names it by design (RPS20)"
  :decided "RPS20 (a), by design as the JVM's AOT (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-24): RPS18-RPS29\")"
  :match [#"^known Clojure's pair, compilation's semantics, as the JVM's AOT"]}
 {:id :compiled-loader-line
  :title "Compiler/LINE in a compiled loader"
  :kind :design
  :why "eval at run time of a form without positions reports Compiler/LINE and COLUMN, which Compiler.load sets for each top-level form but a compiled loader does not (as the JVM's __init class). Recorded as known (doc/FUTAMURA-SURVEY.md, F2's findings, \"the check's own\"); no decision names it by design (RPS20)"
  :decided "RPS20 (a), by design (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-24): RPS18-RPS29\")"
  :match [#"^known Clojure's pair, a position in a message"]}
 {:id :shared-symbols
  :title "symbols shared in a compiled class's constant pool"
  :kind :design
  :why "a class's symbols without metadata are made once (SA155), so two equal quoted symbols of compiled code are identical; Clojure leaves symbols' identity unspecified"
  :decided "doc/FUTAMURA-SURVEY.md, F3.3 (a) (the user, 2026-10-17)"
  :match [#"^known Clojure's pair, the compiled constants \(SA155\)"]}
 {:id :q1-compiled-prims
  :title "compiled fns are primitive where the evaluator's are not (Q1)"
  :kind :design
  :why "a ^long fn compiled implements IFn$LL and IFn$LOL as on the JVM; evaluated it is a fn made at run time, which does not (the eval level's Q1)"
  :decided "doc/go/EVAL-PLAN.md, Q1 (a) (the user, 2026-10-09)"
  :match [#"^known Clojure's pair, native\.ae's copy \(c2j:\), by design of the evaluator"]}
 {:id :identity-hash
  :title "identity hashes (not reproducible)"
  :kind :design
  :why "a StringBuilder's identity hash differs in each run"
  :decided "doc/go/EVAL-NOTES.md, phase 2B (as decided for #object printing)"
  :match [#"^known Clojure's pair, not reproducible: an identity hash"]}
 ;; the suite compiled (bin/clojure-tests --aot, test/arbace-go-aot-results.edn; REAP3, "As built: REAP3", RPS45 (a))
 ;; the suite: namespaces and tests that do not run (the eval level's, the same decisions)
 {:id :gen-class
  :title "gen-class at run time"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "gen-class is a no-op (arbace/genclass.ae): genclass's namespace and its fixture genclass.examples (whose gen-class'd classes it imports) do not load; gen-interface, proxy and deftype make classes at run time over Compiler$Dyn"
  :decided "CDR3's first stage built on branch clojure-cdr (doc/VENDOR-NOTES.md, hand change 31): the AOT reference unskips genclass after the night's run; doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6, \"Not to be done (the user, 2026-10-10)\"; CDR3 (the user, 2026-11-05): gen-class in two stages, doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.(genclass|genclass\.examples): "]}
 {:id :xml
  :title "XML: SAX (arbace.xml)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "arbace.xml loads but parses nothing: SAX (java.xml's xerces closure) is not in the shipped world, so clojure-xml's one test errs at SAXParserFactory"
  :decided "built when the night's measurement of the closure is under 10 MB (doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md, \"As built\"); doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6, \"Not to be done (the user, 2026-10-10)\"; CDR5 (the user, 2026-11-05): SAX and StAX in the shipped world if the growth is under 10 MB, doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.clojure-xml: "]}
 {:id :serialization
  :title "Java serialization (ObjectOutputStream)"
  :kind :design
  :why "java.io.ObjectOutputStream and ObjectInputStream are not in the Go build: serialization's namespace, and java-interop's test-proxy-non-serializable (which also needs arbace.inspector's Swing list-model)"
  :decided "doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6; doc/go/J2G-SPEC.md §12; CDR6 (the user, 2026-11-05): a 2-day spike, then the user's decision, doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.serialization: "
          #"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/test-proxy-non-serializable: "]}
 {:id :desktop
  :title "java.desktop: java.awt.Point and Color"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "java-interop's test-dot (java.awt.Point) and test-bean (java.awt.Color): java.desktop is not in the Go build"
  :decided "built on branch clojure-cdr (doc/go/JRT-NOTES.md, \"Modules\"), closed by the night's conversion and build; doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6; CDR4 (b) (the user, 2026-11-05): Point, Point2D and an sRGB Color in the shipped world, doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/(test-bean|test-dot): "]}
 {:id :tools-deps
  :title "tools.deps' jars (arbace.repl.deps)"
  :kind :design
  :why "arbace.repl.deps adds libraries' jars to the class path at run time (tools.deps); the Go build loads no jars"
  :decided "doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6, \"Not to be done (the user, 2026-10-10)\"; CDR9 (the user, 2026-11-05)"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.repl\.deps: "]}
 {:id :fixtures-excluded-upstream
  :title "fixture namespaces upstream's runner excludes"
  :kind :design
  :why "compilation.load-ns and ns-libs-load-later are fixtures their tests load, not test namespaces (upstream's run_test.clj leaves them out)"
  :decided "upstream's src/script/run_test.clj (clojure/clojure 98d735fab02f)"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.(compilation\.load-ns|ns-libs-load-later): "]}
 {:id :javadoc-url
  :title "java.javadoc's javadoc-url-test: java.sql.Connection is not in the Go build"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "javadoc-url-test's java.sql.Connection assertion errs at Class/forName, compiled as evaluated: java.sql is not in the Go build's world (D6). Its other two errors (Class.getModule) are fixed by jrt's java.lang.Module (RPS55 (a), doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"As built: RPS55\"); the namespace runs at the AOT level since REAP8's record (RPS82 (a))"
  :decided "CDR4 (b) (the user, 2026-11-05): java.sql in the shipped world, built on branch clojure-cdr (doc/go/JRT-NOTES.md, \"Modules\"), closed by the night's conversion and build; doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6; RPS55 (a): the java.sql assertion by design (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-25): RPS40-RPS59\"); RPS82 (a): recorded at the AOT level (\"Decided (2026-10-25): RPS80-RPS82\")"
  :match [#"^error clojure\.test-clojure\.java\.javadoc/javadoc-url-test \(fail 0, error 1\)"]}
 {:id :class-files
  :title "class files: the Go build writes and reads none"
  :kind :design
  :why "compile writes no class files and ASM is gone, at the AOT level too (its compiled classes are the program's, translated by j2g): test-proxy-method-order reads the proxy's class file with ASM (clj-1208, by design at the eval level, is deferred here: :clj-1208)"
  :decided "doc/STANDALONE-SURVEY.md D13; doc/VENDOR-NOTES.md, hand change 23"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/test-proxy-method-order: "]}
 {:id :clj-1208
  :title "compilation's clj-1208: a compiled deftype's static initializer loading its namespace"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "clj-1208 constructs compilation.load-ns's deftype before its namespace is loaded, expecting the class's static initializer to load it (the JVM's AOT class). At the AOT level the deftype is c2j's class, translated by j2g: whether c2j can emit an initializer that loads the namespace is not yet read (doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md, class 9); one case, deferred"
  :decided "CDR8 (b) (the user, 2026-11-05): by design at the eval level (:class-files), deferred at the AOT level, doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.compilation/clj-1208: "]}
 {:id :xml-stream
  :title "javax.xml.stream (reflect's invoke-checks-accessibility)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the test reflects over javax.xml.stream's classes, which are not in the Go build's world (java.xml stays out of the shipped world, D6; the SAX cut, RPS56)"
  :decided "CDR5 (the user, 2026-11-05): SAX and StAX in the shipped world if the growth is under 10 MB, doc/CLOJURE-DESIGN-REVIEW.md; RPS134 (b), doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, Decided (2026-10-28)"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.reflect/invoke-checks-accessibility: "]}
 ;; the suite: tests that fail (at both levels)
 {:id :q1-evaluated
  :title "code the tests evaluate at run time: the evaluator's fns are boxed (Q1)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "primitive-return-decl and incorrect-primitive-type-hint-throws evaluate their code at run time (eval-in-temp-ns, load-string), at the AOT level too: the evaluator's fn is one Go type calling invoke, no IFn primitive interface, so no recur-mismatch warning and no \"Cannot coerce long to int\" (the eval level's :q1-boxed-prims)"
  :decided "CDR2 (a) (the user, 2026-11-05): the evaluator's typing, built on branch clojure-cdr (doc/VENDOR-NOTES.md, hand change 32), closed by the night's build; doc/go/EVAL-PLAN.md, Q1 (a) (the user, 2026-10-09)"
  :match [#"^fail clojure\.test-clojure\.compilation/(primitive-return-decl|incorrect-primitive-type-hint-throws) "]}
 ;; the suite: the AOT level's own
 {:id :runtime-source
  :title "a source the test writes at run time loads from source"
  :kind :design
  :why "compilation's CLJ-1184-do-in-non-list-test spits clojure/bad_def_test.clj and compiles it (arbace.core/compile) while it runs: no compiled loader can exist for a file made after the program was built, so the AOT level loads it from source (test/suite_aot_hook.ae's evaluated, test/arbace-go-aot-results.edn's :evaluated)."
  :decided "by design (the user, 2026-11-02)"
  :match [#"^not-compiled clojure/bad_def_test\.clj: "]}
]
